{"componentChunkName":"component---src-templates-post-template-tsx","path":"/posts/2019-01-19---Evaluating-Chrome-Devtools/","result":{"data":{"markdownRemark":{"id":"8fe69ee3-44e8-5290-af28-a9a4fc901cac","html":"<p>While debugging with some <code class=\"language-text\">console.log</code> statements I noticed that the values logged seemed to differ from what they initially said. Upon uncollapsing the log entry it would consistently show a <code class=\"language-text\">NaN</code> value for some property values while it clearly stated the proper value above it.</p>\n<p><span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n      style=\"position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 960px; \"\n    >\n      <a\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-link\"\n    href=\"/static/827ff2858062ac2c4198046cce6b994d/60b3a/console-log.png\"\n    style=\"display: block\"\n    target=\"_blank\"\n    rel=\"noopener\"\n  >\n    <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n    style=\"padding-bottom: 31.666666666666664%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n  ></span>\n  <picture>\n          <source\n              srcset=\"/static/827ff2858062ac2c4198046cce6b994d/8ac56/console-log.webp 240w,\n/static/827ff2858062ac2c4198046cce6b994d/d3be9/console-log.webp 480w,\n/static/827ff2858062ac2c4198046cce6b994d/e46b2/console-log.webp 960w,\n/static/827ff2858062ac2c4198046cce6b994d/58f5f/console-log.webp 1179w\"\n              sizes=\"(max-width: 960px) 100vw, 960px\"\n              type=\"image/webp\"\n            />\n          <source\n            srcset=\"/static/827ff2858062ac2c4198046cce6b994d/8ff5a/console-log.png 240w,\n/static/827ff2858062ac2c4198046cce6b994d/e85cb/console-log.png 480w,\n/static/827ff2858062ac2c4198046cce6b994d/d9199/console-log.png 960w,\n/static/827ff2858062ac2c4198046cce6b994d/60b3a/console-log.png 1179w\"\n            sizes=\"(max-width: 960px) 100vw, 960px\"\n            type=\"image/png\"\n          />\n          <img\n            class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n            src=\"/static/827ff2858062ac2c4198046cce6b994d/d9199/console-log.png\"\n            alt=\"Console output\"\n            title=\"\"\n            loading=\"lazy\"\n            decoding=\"async\"\n            style=\"width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;\"\n          />\n        </picture>\n  </a>\n    </span></p>\n<p>As it turns out this is caused by Chrome re-evaluating the object with the data it has at the moment you uncollapse it rather than just showing you what the values were at that moment in time. There is a small info icon that does aim to explain this behaviour but its wording does not really clarify the most important aspect, which is that it re-evaluates it without the original context.</p>\n<p>We can quickly verify this behaviour ourselves by defining an object, logging it and making a change to the object prior to uncollapsing:</p>\n<p><img src=\"/2b917fed2abcdb1ce14a216f70da00d0/demo-initial.png\" alt=\"Declaring an object\"></p>\n<p>Change a value on the object:</p>\n<p><img src=\"/b99803a6e89c5daf98a27b7e300a6b21/demo-action.png\" alt=\"Change property value\"></p>\n<p>If we now uncollapse the previous log statement, we can see it got re-evaluated based on our current context</p>\n<p><img src=\"/093fba728f79ad28128d2d4e8cab31ff/demo-result.png\" alt=\"Uncollapse log statement\"></p>\n<p>Interestingly it looks like the evaluation is only done on the first collapse: subsequent alterations to the property and collapsing/uncollapsing does not change the existing log statement.</p>","fields":{"slug":"/posts/2019-01-19---Evaluating-Chrome-Devtools/","tagSlugs":["/tag/java-script/","/tag/google-chrome/","/tag/debugging/"]},"frontmatter":{"date":"2019-01-19T00:03:00.000Z","tags":["JavaScript","Google Chrome","Debugging"],"title":"Evaluating Chrome Devtools","description":"Simple console log statements are not as innocent as they might seem.","socialImage":null}}},"pageContext":{"slug":"/posts/2019-01-19---Evaluating-Chrome-Devtools/"}},"staticQueryHashes":["4208939363"],"slicesMap":{}}